<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  diskarbitrationd preferences (nextbsd-userland#199).

  Nothing on NextBSD publishes the console user yet (State:/Users/ConsoleUser,
  /usr/libexec/consoleuser), so removable and external media mount without a
  login, owned by root, as they did before the console-user port.
  AutomountDisksWithoutUserLogin also marks external media trusted on Apple;
  DAMountTrustExternal false keeps NextBSD's untrusted options (nosuid,
  noatime) for them.

  Once a login program runs "consoleuser set <user>" / "consoleuser clear",
  delete AutomountDisksWithoutUserLogin (and DAMountTrustExternal) for Apple's
  defaults: removable and external media wait for a login. Setting it to false
  is Apple's other mode: removable media wait, external media mount at boot,
  trusted. See diskarbitrationd(8).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>AutomountDisksWithoutUserLogin</key>
	<true/>
	<key>DAMountTrustExternal</key>
	<false/>
</dict>
</plist>
